<title>NORWAY: Dyno posts H197 pre-tax up 40 pct.</title>
<headline>Dyno posts H197 pre-tax up 40 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30.</p>
<p>				 (millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p>  Operating result		 300	vs	  244</p>
<p>  Pre-tax profits		  262	vs	  187</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Norwegian explosives and chemicals company is Dyno Industrier ASA. A Reuters poll of seven analysts forecast an operating result of 254 million crowns and pre-tax profits of 218 million crowns.  </p>
<p>  Operating income	     5,531	vs	4,312</p>
<p>Operating expenses before</p>
<p>		    depreciation 4,974	vs	4,246</p>
<p>  Depreciation		     257	vs	  231</p>
<p>Earnings from associated</p>
<p>		    companies	  4	vs	    2</p>
<p>  Net financial costs	     42	vs	   59</p>
<p>  Tax				   94	vs	   63</p>
<p>  Minorities			  20	vs	   13</p>
<p>  Corporate result		 148	vs	  111</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
